<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Australia Act 1986</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> Act 1986 comprises matching laws of the Australian and British parliaments that took effect on 3 March 1986. They ended the British Parliament's power to legislate for Australia and its states, removed remaining British involvement in state government and abolished appeals from Australian courts to the Privy Council in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, completing Australia's legal independence.</p></div>
